From 1261e4e971f3514a2d197df4a8a6cd223e15b5c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lbh <lbh@sapcemit.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 21:24:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] fix(egl): add PVR vendor driver filter for GLVND
 multi-vendor coexistence

Restrict PVR EGL vendor to only claim PVR/spacemit DRM devices via
dri2_pvr_is_supported_driver(). Without this, the PVR vendor (priority
40) claims AMD/Intel devices and blocks system mesa via GLVND.

Three-layer defense: eglQueryDevicesEXT enumeration (egldevice.c),
getPlatformDisplay early rejection (eglglvnd.c), and per-platform
eglInitialize filter (wayland/drm/surfaceless/device/x11/x11_dri3).
---
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c             | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.h             |  7 ++++++
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_device.c      |  6 +++++
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_drm.c         |  8 ++++++
 src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c |  9 +++++++
